abstract: >-
  We construct natural-number arithmetic on correlation modes together with
  source-weighted dynamics of its generating expressions. Minimal unbiased
  compositional change determines a rotation plane and a Gaussian law. Local
  information and total normalized correlation determine a finite window. Within the
  separated nondegenerate homogeneous local boundary class, preservation of constants
  selects the Neumann closure. Modulation and composition of the oriented modes give
  an ordered Peano semiring with unique factorization, quadratic energy and canonical
  scale transport. Winding degree certifies the arithmetic. Each natural value has a
  finite expression fibre. Equal root-channel weights and independent child assembly
  define a positive history law with the original Gaussian marginal. Conditional
  readout separates value information from history variation. The same weights on
  parent–child relations define a nonnegative self-adjoint trace-class assembly
  operator with explicit Gaussian cutoff bounds. A history difference at value four
  has zero initial readout but a strictly nonzero subsequent value response under the
  complete operator. This coupling persists under small changes of the relevant
  conditional weights. Eliminating history differences gives an exact memory equation
  and a joint norm budget. Signed balances, fractions and certified limits extend the
  scalar field. The natural-mode arithmetic, finite-fibre history law and assembly
  results have accompanying Lean formalizations.
